officials believe russian hackers are  behind another major campaign against  u.s government agencies  non-governmental organizations and think  tanks  state department correspondent rich  edson tells us tonight experts believe  it's the same group  responsible for a previous high-profile  attack  russian hackers have hit the u.s  government again  microsoft says the same russian  government-backed cyber operatives  responsible for last year's solar winds  hack infiltrated an email system at the  state department's development agency  and targeted quote government agencies  think tanks consultants  and non-governmental organizations  approximately 3  000 email accounts at more than 150  different organizations  all this less than three weeks ahead of  president biden's summit with russian  president vladimir putin  the ransomware attack by criminal  hackers  earlier this month well that was a  warning shot  so we must defend our nation against  these threats some in congress say the  administration needs to respond to this  latest attack  house intelligence committee chairman  adam schiff says quote russia remains  undeterred despite sanctions following  the solar winds attack  those sanctions gave the administration  flexibility to tighten the economic  screws further if necessary  it now appears necessary microsoft says  the hackers  accessed the u.s agency for  international development's marketing  service  then they used it to send legitimate  looking emails like this  to thousands of accounts clicking on the  link in the email  gives the cyber spys access to computer  systems  these emails went out as recently as  this week  and at least a quarter of the targeted  organizations work in international  development  humanitarian aid and human rights biden  has promised to get tough on russia  republicans have recently criticized the  president for even agreeing to a summit  with the russian president  and for the administration refusing  sanctions on the company building the  nordstrom 2 pipeline  the white house says despite the hack  there are no changes to the biden putin  summit  scheduled for june 16th in switzerland  brent  we'll be there rich edson live the state  department rich thanks hey sean hannity  here hey  click here to subscribe to fox news  youtube page  and catch our hottest interviews and  most compelling analysis  you will not get it anywhere else
 

